The Mercedes-Benz C-Class C300de is a plug-in hybrid diesel variant of the current W206 generation. It combines a diesel engine with an electric motor and a large battery.

Here's an evaluation based on the provided data and scoring guide:

*   **price\_usd**: Plug-in hybrid variants are typically more expensive than standard internal combustion engine models. While specific USD pricing for the C300de is not readily available, the standard W206 C-Class starts significantly above the $35,000 market average (Source [2]). Given the added hybrid technology and battery, the C300de's price would be considerably higher. Score: -0.60.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: High purchase price, potential for higher maintenance on a complex hybrid system, and potentially higher insurance costs contribute to a high 5-year cost of ownership, although fuel savings from the hybrid system could offset some costs. Score: -0.50.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: Luxury vehicles, especially those with complex powertrains and higher repair costs, typically have higher insurance rates. Score: -0.20.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: Mercedes-Benz maintenance is generally higher than average (Source [14, 33, 44]). The added complexity of a diesel plug-in hybrid system could lead to higher maintenance costs compared to a standard ICE model. Score: -0.70.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: The W206 C-Class has had some reported issues with electronics (Source [11, 13, 23, 24, 25]). While the diesel engine (OM654) is generally reliable, the integration of a complex plug-in hybrid system adds potential points of failure. Score: -0.40.
*   **hp**: Total system output is 309-313 hp (Source [4, 5, 7, 9, 10, 17, 18, 19, 25]). This is well above the 200 hp average. Score: 0.60.
*   **torque**: Total system torque is 700 Nm (516.29 lb-ft) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). This is significantly above the 190 lb-ft average. Score: 0.90.
*   **cylinder\_count**: The internal combustion engine is a 4-cylinder diesel (Source [4, 5, 7, 9, 17]). This is common, so average. Score: 0.00.
*   **engine\_displacement**: The internal combustion engine is 2.0L (1993 cm³) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9, 17]). Around the average for a 4-cylinder engine. Score: 0.00.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Around 5.9-6.2 seconds (Source [4, 5, 7, 9, 18, 19, 25]). This is significantly faster than the 7.5-second average. Score: 0.70.
*   **top\_speed**: Around 146-151 mph (235-243 km/h) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). Around the 150 mph average. Score: 0.00.
*   **drive\_type**: Available in RWD and AWD (4Matic) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). RWD scores +1.00 according to the guide. Score: 1.00.
*   **transmission\_type**: 9-speed automatic (9G-TRONIC) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). This is a modern, smooth automatic. Score: 1.00.
*   **offroad\_ability**: Low ground clearance (around 9.7 cm or 3.8 inches) (Source [7, 9]), sedan body style, not designed for off-road. Score: 1.00 (based on guide examples).
*   **braking\_dist\_ft**: Not explicitly stated for the C300de, but the standard C300 measured 154 ft from 70 mph (Source [2]). This is worse than the 125 ft average from 60 mph. Score: -0.50.
*   **size**: Length is around 4751 mm (187 inches) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). This is slightly larger than the 4600mm average. Score: 0.10.
*   **wheelbase**: 2865 mm (112.8 inches) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). This is longer than the 2700mm average. Score: 0.20.
*   **body\_style**: 4-door Sedan (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). Estate also available (Source [22]). Score: 0.00.
*   **seats**: 5 seats (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). Score: 0.00.
*   **cargo\_space**: 315 liters (11.12 cu ft) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). The large battery significantly reduces trunk space compared to the standard C-Class sedan (455 liters / 16 cu ft) (Source [2, 24]). This is below the 15 cu ft average. Score: -0.50.
*   **rear\_space**: Improved over the previous generation, with more legroom (Source [2, 13]). Score: 0.20.
*   **ground\_clearance\_in**: Around 9.7 cm (3.8 inches) (Source [7, 9]). Low for a sedan by modern standards. Score: -0.20.
*   **turn\_radius\_ft**: 11.07m (36.32 ft) for RWD, 11.45m (37.57 ft) for 4Matic (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). Around the 36 ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **mpg**: Plug-in hybrids have very high claimed fuel economy figures when driven on a mix of electric and fuel power. Combined WLTP is around 0.4-0.6 L/100 km (equivalent to extremely high MPG) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). This is well above the 30 mpg average for a conventional car. Score: 1.00.
*   **co2\_g\_km**: Very low CO2 emissions due to significant electric driving capability. WLTP is around 10-17 g/km (Source [4, 5, 7, 9]). This is well below the 175 g/km average. Score: 0.90.
*   **electric\_range\_mi**: WLTP electric range is around 93-115 km (57.79 - 71.46 miles) (Source [4, 5, 7, 9, 12, 16]). This is a very good electric range for a PHEV. Score: 0.80.
*   **charge\_speed\_kw**: Supports AC charging up to 11 kW and DC fast charging up to 55 kW (Source [7, 9, 17]). 11 kW AC is good, 55 kW DC is decent for a PHEV but not as fast as dedicated EVs. Score: 0.40.
*   **style\_sleek\_vs\_boxy**: Modern sedan design, leaning towards sleek, inspired by the S-Class (Source [2, 13]). Score: 0.40.
*   **style\_aggression\_rating**: Standard C-Class styling is elegant, AMG Line adds aggression. Assuming standard C300de styling. Score: 0.00.
*   **style\_modernity\_rating**: Recent design, looks modern and inspired by the S-Class (Source [2, 13]). Score: 0.80.
*   **handling\_rating**: Capable, but reviews suggest it's focused more on comfort than sporty handling compared to rivals (Source [2, 13, 14]). The added weight of the battery can impact agility (Source [6] - C300d weight mentioned). Score: -0.10.
*   **ride\_comfort\_rating**: Generally praised for excellent ride comfort, a significant improvement over the W205 (Source [2, 13]). PHEV models often have standard comfort suspension and rear air suspension (Source [12]), enhancing ride. Score: 0.80.
*   **cabin\_noise\_rating**: Praised for a quiet and refined cabin, especially when running on electric power (Source [2]). Score: 0.80.
*   **shift\_smooth\_rating**: 9G-Tronic is generally smooth (Source [2, 13]). Integration between the engine and electric motor can sometimes be noticeable, but generally well-executed. Score: 0.50.
*   **steering\_feel\_rating**: Reviews mention a lack of steering feel despite being precise (Source [2, 14]). Score: -0.50.
*   **adas\_score**: Offers a wide range of modern ADAS features, especially with optional packages (Source [2]). Score: 0.60.
*   **visibility\_rating**: Standard sedan visibility. Score: 0.00.
*   **headlight\_rating**: LED High Performance standard, Digital Light optional (Source [2]). Good standard, excellent optional. Score: 0.40.
*   **security\_rating**: Offers advanced security features like fingerprint scanner and enhanced systems (Source [2]). Score: 0.60.
*   **screen\_in**: Large central touchscreen, 11.9 inches standard/optional (Source [2, 13]). Score: 0.80.
*   **infotainment\_ux\_rating**: Latest MBUX system, generally well-regarded but some find touch controls fiddly (Source [2, 13]). Score: 0.60.
*   **smartphone\_connect\_rating**: Wireless Apple CarPlay and Android Auto standard (Source [2, 13]). Score: 1.00.
*   **audio\_rating**: Optional Burmester system is excellent (Source [2]). Standard system is likely average. Score: 0.40.
*   **usb\_ports**: Offers multiple USB-C ports (Source [2]). Score: 0.60.
*   **comfort\_feature\_score**: Heated front seats standard, power seats with memory, dual-zone climate, ambient lighting (Source [2]). PHEV models often have standard rear air suspension (Source [12]). Good level of comfort features. Score: 0.70.
*   **convenience\_feature\_score**: 360-degree camera, self-parking, wireless charging, fingerprint sensor, keyless entry available (Source [2]). Good convenience features. Score: 0.60.
*   **brand\_prestige\_rating**: Mercedes-Benz is a high-prestige brand. Score: 0.80.
*   **model\_prestige\_rating**: C-Class is a core, mid-range model for Mercedes-Benz. Score: 0.00.
*   **trim\_prestige\_rating**: C300de is a high-tech, efficient variant, representing a significant step up from base models, but not a full AMG performance model. Score: -0.20.
*   **interior\_luxury\_rating**: High-quality materials, S-Class inspired design, ambient lighting (Source [2, 13]). Some reviews note mixed material quality in lower areas (Source [2, 13]). Score: 0.70.
*   **interior\_tech\_focus\_rating**: Dominated by large screens, heavy reliance on touch controls, fingerprint scanner, advanced hybrid interface (Source [2, 13]). High tech focus. Score: 0.90.

